# Vendored conformance artifacts are byte-identical copies of upstream KISS
# blobs. Line-ending conversion would silently break that identity — and the
# whole point of vendoring rather than retyping is that the bytes are the
# evidence.
#
# This OVERRIDES the repository root's `*.json text eol=lf` (`.gitattributes`
# line 22), which would otherwise normalize these files. `-text` disables eol
# conversion in BOTH directions, so a Windows checkout still hashes to the
# upstream blob id.
#
# HISTORY: this file is carried forward from `fuel-dispatch/tests/corpus/`,
# deleted by the GAP-273 consolidation. It was INERT at the time of the move
# (every artifact here is already LF-only, and the worktree hashes matched
# HEAD exactly), so nothing broke — but a guard that happens to be unnecessary
# today is not the same object as one that is unnecessary, and the next
# re-vendor of an upstream blob containing CRLF would be normalized silently.
# Widened from one filename to `*.json`: all six artifacts here are byte-
# identity evidence read by tests, and the original covered only one.
*.json -text
